Jar 1 -> Apple
Jar 2 -> Mix of Orange/Apple
Jar 3 -> Orange
So when he says mislablled, it means no way i can say that jar 1 can be apple. According to him, jar 1 can never be apple because it says all are mislabled. Initially the answer i gave was wrong. But the interviewer didnt say that. i asked is that ok, then he said the answer given by me is wrong. So again i gave the answer which was correct but he seemed to be not that impressed.
Solution -> Keep in mind all are mislablled. Jar 2 cannot be mix of orange and apple. Hence take one fruit out of it. Lets say the fruit is orange. Hence jar 2 is definitely orange. Now if jar 2 is orange, that means jar 3 is definitely not orange it can be mix or only apple. Now jar 1 also cannot be only apple as its mislabelled. Hence i can say that jar 3 can be apple and jar 1 can be mix. Hence minimum no of fruits required is 1.

Question 1: Efficient Teams
There are n candidates and a total of n/2 teams to be formed. Each candidate has a skill level denoted by skill[i]. Make teams so that the total skill is the same and return the sum of efficiencies
If there is no way to create the teams that satisfy these conditions, return -1.
Efficiency is calculated like this:

Efficiency of team [1, 3] = 1* 3 = 3
Efficiency of team [2, 2] = 2 * 2 =  4
Example:
The skills of the candidates are skill = [1, 2, 3, 2] so they can be paired as [1, 3], [2, 2].

Efficiency:[ 1, 3] = 1* 3 = 3
Efficiency: [2, 2] = 2 * 2 = 4

Should return the sum of efficiencies: 3 + 4 = 7

My approach:

sumOfEachPair = sum(all skills) / (number of candidates) * 2
Create a hashmap to store differences
Create accumulator to keep track of sum of efficiencies
Iterate through each candidate’s skill:
if the skill is larger than the sum of each pair, return -1 early
if the current skill is in the hashmap
add to accumulator: (skill * (sumOfEachPair - skill)
decrement key value of key = (sumOfEachPair - skill) by 1 and delete the key value pair if it equals 0
if the current skill is not in the hashmap:
create a key value pair with key = (sumOfEachPair - skill) and set the value to 1
return the accumulator variable if hasmap is empty, other wise return -1
This passed all the test cases available.

Time: O(n) , one pass
Space: O(n) , hashmap to store all the differences

