The digit 1 only appears in groups of size one group, if it appears at all. For example, for one group = 2, "011110110" satisfies this condition while "01101010" does not.
The digit 0 only appears in groups of size zero_group, if it appears at all. For example, for zero group = 3, "11" satisfies this condition while "101010" does not. For example, for one group = 2, zero group = 1, the strings "011", "000" are good while the strings "001" and "111" are not.
Given four integers:

min_length: min length of a valid string
max_length: max length of a valid string
one_group: group size of digit 1
zero_group: group size of digit 0
min length = 1, max length = 3, one group = 2 and zero group = 1. The good strings satisfying the criteria are: (“0”, “00”, "11", "011", "110", "000"]. Hence, the result is 6.

int countGoodStrings(int min_length, int max_length, int one_group, int zero_group){
    vector<long long int> dp(max_length+1, 0);
    long long int res = 0;
    dp[0] = 1;
    for(int i=1;i<= max_length;i++){
        if(i>=zero_group){
            dp[i] += dp[i-zero_group];
        }
        if(i>=one_group){
            dp[i] += dp[i-one_group];
        }
        dp[i] %= (1000000007);
    }
    for(int i=min_length; i<= max_length; i++){
        res += dp[i] % (1000000007);
    }

    return (int)(res % (1000000007));
}